   "q": "<style>.katex-display{overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:hidden;padding:2px 0}</style><span style=\"display:block;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:8px\">Repeat Assessment · 1 Feb 2024 · Part I (a) · 4 pts</span><span style=\"display:block;font-size:17px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.5\">The (maximal) domain of \\(f : D_f\\to\\mathbb{R}\\) defined by $$f(x,y)=\\frac{\\sqrt{y-x^2}}{\\ln(x^2+y^2)}$$ is the set <br>\\(D_f=\\) <span style=\"display:inline-block;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:5px;padding:0 6px;margin:0 2px;font-size:.78em;line-height:1.35;font-weight:700;vertical-align:.08em\">1</span></span><details style=\"margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted)\">Show original exam item</summary><img src=\"img/feb24-a.png\" alt=\"Original exam item a\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;margin-top:8px;border-radius:8px;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line)\"></details>",
   "a": "<p><span style=\"display:inline-block;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:5px;padding:0 6px;margin:0 2px;font-size:.78em;line-height:1.35;font-weight:700;vertical-align:.08em\">1</span> \\(\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb{R}^2 : y\\ge x^2 \\ \\wedge\\ x^2+y^2>0 \\ \\wedge\\ x^2+y^2\\ne1\\}\\)</p><p><p><i>\\(\\sqrt{\\ }\\) needs \\(y-x^2\\ge0\\); ln needs \\(x^2+y^2>0\\); the denominator needs \\(\\ln(x^2+y^2)\\ne0\\), i.e. \\(x^2+y^2\\ne1\\).</i></p></p>"
