   "qHtml": true,
   "q": "<style>.katex-display{overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:hidden;padding:2px 0}</style><span style=\"display:block;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:8px\">Repeat Assessment · 1 Feb 2024 · Part I (d) · 4 pts</span><span style=\"display:block;font-size:17px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.5\">With respect to a map \\(f:\\mathbb{R}^2\\to\\mathbb{R}\\), one knows that \\(\\nabla f(x,y)=(-2x\\sin(x^2+y);-\\sin(x^2+y))\\).<br>If \\(f(x,y)\\) does not have constant terms in both components, then $$f(x,y)=\\boxed{1}$$</span><details style=\"margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted)\">Show original exam item</summary><img src=\"img/feb24-d.png\" alt=\"Original exam item d\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;margin-top:8px;border-radius:8px;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line)\"></details>",
