   "src": "Feb 2024 · I(e)",
   "type": "open",
   "qHtml": true,
   "q": "<style>.katex-display{overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:hidden;padding:2px 0}</style><span style=\"display:block;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:8px\">Repeat Assessment · 1 Feb 2024 · Part I (e) · 4 pts</span><span style=\"display:block;font-size:17px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.5\">If \\(u_n=\\left(\\ln\\left(1-\\dfrac{1}{2n+1}\\right)^{n+\\frac12};\\dfrac1n\\right)\\), \\(n\\in\\mathbb{N}\\) and \\(f(x,y)=-2x+\\cos y\\), then$$\\lim_{n\\to+\\infty}f(u_n)=\\boxed{1}$$</span><details style=\"margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted)\">Show original exam item</summary><img src=\"img/feb24-e.png\" alt=\"Original exam item e\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;margin-top:8px;border-radius:8px;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line)\"></details>",
   "a": "<p><span style=\"display:inline-block;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:5px;padding:0 6px;margin:0 2px;font-size:.78em;line-height:1.35;font-weight:700;vertical-align:.08em\">1</span> \\(2\\)</p><p><p><i>\\(\\left(1-\\frac{1}{2n+1}\\right)^{\\frac{2n+1}{2}}\\to e^{-1/2}\\), so the first coordinate goes to \\(-\\frac12\\) and the second to 0. Then \\(f\\to-2\\cdot(-\\tfrac12)+\\cos0=1+1=2\\).</i></p></p>"
