   "src": "Feb 2024 · I(h)",
   "type": "open",
   "qHtml": true,
   "q": "<style>.katex-display{overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:hidden;padding:2px 0}</style><span style=\"display:block;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:8px\">Repeat Assessment · 1 Feb 2024 · Part I (h) · 4 pts</span><span style=\"display:block;font-size:17px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.5\">With respect to the \\(C^2\\) map \\(f:\\mathbb{R}^2\\to\\mathbb{R}\\), we know that \\(\\nabla f(3,2)=(0,0)\\) and$$H_f(3,2)=\\begin{pmatrix}-5 & \\boxed{1}\\\\ 0 & \\boxed{2}\\end{pmatrix}.$$Then, we conclude that \\((3,2)\\) is a local <b>maximizer</b> of \\(f\\).</span><details style=\"margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted)\">Show original exam item</summary><img src=\"img/feb24-h.png\" alt=\"Original exam item h\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;margin-top:8px;border-radius:8px;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line)\"></details>",
   "a": "<p><span style=\"display:inline-block;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:5px;padding:0 6px;margin:0 2px;font-size:.78em;line-height:1.35;font-weight:700;vertical-align:.08em\">1</span> \\(0\\) (the Hessian is symmetric)</p><p><span style=\"display:inline-block;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:5px;padding:0 6px;margin:0 2px;font-size:.78em;line-height:1.35;font-weight:700;vertical-align:.08em\">2</span> \\(-3\\) (for instance: any negative number)</p><p><p><i>\\(\\begin{pmatrix}-5&0\\\\0&-3\\end{pmatrix}\\) is negative definite → local maximum.</i></p></p>"
