   "src": "Feb 2024 · I(i)",
   "type": "open",
   "qHtml": true,
   "q": "<style>.katex-display{overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:hidden;padding:2px 0}</style><span style=\"display:block;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:8px\">Repeat Assessment · 1 Feb 2024 · Part I (i) · 4 pts</span><span style=\"display:block;font-size:17px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.5\">Consider the following utility <b>maximisation</b> problem. There are two goods and an agent with income 3 who wishes to maximize the utility:$$U(x,y)=\\ln(x+1)+y,$$ $$x\\ge0,\\quad y\\ge0$$subject to a budget constraint \\(\\frac12x+y\\le3\\). The necessary conditions to solve the utility maximization problem are:$$\\begin{cases}\\boxed{1}-\\frac12\\mu_1+\\mu_2=0\\\\ \\boxed{2}-\\mu_1+\\mu_3=0\\\\ \\mu_1x=0,\\ \\mu_2y=0\\\\ \\boxed{3}=0\\\\ \\mu_1,\\,\\mu_2,\\,\\mu_3\\ \\boxed{4}\\ 0\\\\ \\frac12x+y\\le3\\\\ x\\ge0,y\\ge0\\end{cases}$$</span><details style=\"margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted)\">Show original exam item</summary><img src=\"img/feb24-i.png\" alt=\"Original exam item i\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;margin-top:8px;border-radius:8px;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line)\"></details>",
   "a": "<p><span style=\"display:inline-block;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:5px;padding:0 6px;margin:0 2px;font-size:.78em;line-height:1.35;font-weight:700;vertical-align:.08em\">1</span> \\(\\dfrac{1}{x+1}\\)</p><p><span style=\"display:inline-block;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:5px;padding:0 6px;margin:0 2px;font-size:.78em;line-height:1.35;font-weight:700;vertical-align:.08em\">2</span> \\(1\\)</p><p><span style=\"display:inline-block;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:5px;padding:0 6px;margin:0 2px;font-size:.78em;line-height:1.35;font-weight:700;vertical-align:.08em\">3</span> \\(\\mu_3\\left(\\frac12x+y-3\\right)\\)</p><p><span style=\"display:inline-block;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:5px;padding:0 6px;margin:0 2px;font-size:.78em;line-height:1.35;font-weight:700;vertical-align:.08em\">4</span> \\(\\ge\\)</p><p><p><i>Answers as in the official solution.</i></p></p><p><p><i>⚠ Check: the printed system mixes up the multipliers. From the first two lines, \\(\\mu_1\\) multiplies the budget (coefficients \\(\\frac12\\) and 1), \\(\\mu_2\\) goes with \\(x\\) and \\(\\mu_3\\) with \\(y\\). So the consistent conditions would be \\(\\mu_1(\\frac12x+y-3)=0\\), \\(\\mu_2x=0\\), \\(\\mu_3y=0\\). Fill in the blanks as the official key does, but know why.</i></p></p>"
