   "q": "<style>.katex-display{overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:hidden;padding:2px 0}</style><span style=\"display:block;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:8px\">Repeat Assessment · 1 Feb 2024 · Part I (j) · 4 pts</span><span style=\"display:block;font-size:17px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.5\">The map \\(y(x)=\\cos(4x)\\), \\(x\\in\\mathbb{R}\\), is a solution of the IVP $$\\begin{cases}y''=\\boxed{1}\\\\ y(\\boxed{2})=0\\end{cases}$$</span><details style=\"margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted)\">Show original exam item</summary><img src=\"img/feb24-j.png\" alt=\"Original exam item j\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;margin-top:8px;border-radius:8px;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line)\"></details>",
   "a": "<p><span style=\"display:inline-block;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:5px;padding:0 6px;margin:0 2px;font-size:.78em;line-height:1.35;font-weight:700;vertical-align:.08em\">1</span> \\(-16\\cos(4x)\\) or \\(-16y\\)</p><p><span style=\"display:inline-block;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:5px;padding:0 6px;margin:0 2px;font-size:.78em;line-height:1.35;font-weight:700;vertical-align:.08em\">2</span> \\(\\pi/8\\)</p><p><p><i>\\(\\cos(4\\cdot\\frac{\\pi}{8})=\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{2}=0\\). (The handwritten solution writes \\(y'\\), but it means \\(y''\\).)</i></p></p>"
