   "type": "open",
   "qHtml": true,
   "q": "<style>.katex-display{overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:hidden;padding:2px 0}</style><span style=\"display:block;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:8px\">Resit Assessment · 8 Jan 2026 · Part I (b) · 7 pts</span><span style=\"display:block;font-size:17px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.5\">With respect to the set <br>\\(\\Omega=\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb{R}^2 : |x-5|<1\\ \\wedge\\ 4\\le y<7\\}\\cup\\{(0,0)\\},\\)<br>we may conclude that \\((0,0)\\) is not a/an <span style=\"display:inline-block;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:5px;padding:0 6px;margin:0 2px;font-size:.78em;line-height:1.35;font-weight:700;vertical-align:.08em\">1</span> point of \\(\\Omega\\),<br>\\(int(\\Omega)=\\{\\)<span style=\"display:inline-block;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:5px;padding:0 6px;margin:0 2px;font-size:.78em;line-height:1.35;font-weight:700;vertical-align:.08em\">2</span>\\(\\}\\),<br>and, since \\(int(\\Omega)\\ne\\Omega\\), then \\(\\Omega\\) is not <span style=\"display:inline-block;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:5px;padding:0 6px;margin:0 2px;font-size:.78em;line-height:1.35;font-weight:700;vertical-align:.08em\">3</span></span><details style=\"margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted)\">Show original exam item</summary><img src=\"img/jan26-b.png\" alt=\"Original exam item b\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;margin-top:8px;border-radius:8px;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line)\"></details>",
   "a": "<p><span style=\"display:inline-block;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:5px;padding:0 6px;margin:0 2px;font-size:.78em;line-height:1.35;font-weight:700;vertical-align:.08em\">1</span> <b>interior</b> / <b>accumulation</b> (it is an isolated point)</p><p><span style=\"display:inline-block;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:5px;padding:0 6px;margin:0 2px;font-size:.78em;line-height:1.35;font-weight:700;vertical-align:.08em\">2</span> \\((x,y)\\in\\mathbb{R}^2 : |x-5|<1\\ \\wedge\\ 4<y<7\\)</p><p><span style=\"display:inline-block;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:5px;padding:0 6px;margin:0 2px;font-size:.78em;line-height:1.35;font-weight:700;vertical-align:.08em\">3</span> <b>open</b></p>"
